        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T16:12:38Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): refuse a picked contour ring whose side stands in the part\n\nA 2D Contour with Side Outside on a picked hole wall walked only the\npart top plane: the depth ladder reads the material strictly above each\nlevel, and nothing stands above the top. The operation posted with no\nwarning and machined nothing the user picked.\n\nPicked rings (the Selection source) now go through contour_on_picked.\npicked_law refuses by name a ring that walks no level below its local\npart top while the operation levels go below that top, and names the\nfix (Inside or Auto for a hole, Outside or Auto for a block outline).\nThe whole-model source is unchanged.\n\nFixes #1927\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
