        "date": "2026-11-15T19:22:45Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): name an unreadable mesh, not the side, in the picked-ring refusal\n\nThe depth ladder now keeps, per ring, the slice error that stopped it\n(Ladder::unread). picked_law still refuses a picked ring that keeps only\nthe top plane. When the part could not be sectioned under that ring (a\nself-touching shell), the refusal names that error and the skipped\nlevels. It no longer tells the user to change Side.\n\nsetup_align: the refusal was correct in the setup frame. Flipped over Y,\nthe hole ring of the top annulus stands in solid material at Z 16 and\nZ 12. The test now picks the modelled bottom face with Side Outside and\nasserts a cut below the top. It keeps the annulus as a control that\ngenerates as modelled and is refused once flipped.\n\nstitch_cross: asserts the named refusal, the skipped level, the\nnon-manifold cause, and that the side is not blamed.\n\nRefs #1927\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
